  "integrationInstances.createInstance": "Insert the typed record. With id it is stored under that id (a duplicate id is refused); without one the PROVIDER mints it and answers it. kind picks one of describe().kinds.",
  "integrationInstances.deleteInstance": "Delete the record and its keychain refs together. For an instance that brings devices the hub also removes the integration's devices (their tombstones, D865), the registry row, and emits IntegrationDeleted; a fixed builtin and an instance a link names are refused first.",
  "integrationInstances.describe": "What kind of instances this addon's integration holds and how to configure them.",
  "integrationInstances.getInstance": "Fetch one integration instance by id; null when absent.",
  "integrationInstances.instanceFormSchema": "The form; id: null is the create form.",
  "integrationInstances.listInstances": "List the integration's instances (accounts, relays, destinations).",
  "integrationInstances.setInstanceEnabled": "Switch ONE instance on or off, for every role; a missing record is created from the addon's initial body. A row control, not a form field: updateInstance.values is the form patch (D62, D996). An off instance keeps its record and secrets and does no work.",
  "integrationInstances.testInstance": "Test an instance's connection with the given values before saving.",
  "integrationInstances.updateInstance": "Create or change an integration instance.",
  "integrations.adoptInstanceRows": "The one-time move of an addon's switches into the registry (D1066): for each instance record the addon holds, an absent row is created as a services row under the addon-minted id, and a row that disagrees with a STATED body switch is corrected (a body that states nothing never moves an existing row). A row that belongs to another addon is left alone and returned in conflicts (the caller keeps its own copy of that state), and an addon naming another addon's id is refused FORBIDDEN. Idempotent: a rerun changes nothing. It never notifies the addon.",
  "integrations.delete": "Delete an integration from the hub side: its devices, its registry row and its record, and announce it. It works while the addon that owns the instance is down (installed but crashed), where integration-instances.deleteInstance has no provider to route to; with the provider up the record is removed through it as well. A fixed builtin and an instance a link names are refused first.",
  "integrations.get": "Fetch one integration with its state.",
  "integrations.getAvailableTypes": "List the integration types that can be added.",
  "integrations.getByAddonId": "The devices-role row of an addon; a services instance row never answers for its addon.",
  "integrations.list": "List the integrations with their current state.",
  "integrations.listByAddon": "Every registry row of one addon, services instances included: the addon reads its own switches with it at boot (D1066). A pure registry read; the Integrations list (list) hides the rows of a services instance, this does not.",
  "integrations.update": "Change an integration's settings.",
  "intercom.endTalkSession": "Close the raw-PCM talk session. Idempotent.",
  "intercom.getStatus": "The device's current status as reported by this capability; null when unknown.",
  "intercom.handleAnswer": "Pass the viewer's SDP answer to an open two-way audio session.",
  "intercom.pushTalkAudio": "Push one chunk of talk-back audio onto the active talk session. The cap is codec-agnostic: the caller declares (or omits) the wire format via codec; the provider decides between passthrough (when the wire codec matches the camera's native talk channel), transcoding via the audio-codec cap, or rejecting the call.",
  "intercom.startSession": "Open a server-side WebRTC audio-only session. Returns an SDP offer with a single sendonly audio m-line the client answers (client → server direction). The server wakes battery cams transparently before opening the upstream talk channel.",
  "intercom.startTalkSession": "Open a raw-PCM talk session (no WebRTC SDP plumbing). Used by non-WebRTC consumers (HomeKit export, Alexa raw audio, test harnesses) that already have decoded PCM frames and just need a direct path onto the camera's talk channel. Mutually exclusive with startSession (an active WebRTC session must be stopped before a raw-PCM session can be opened on the same device, and vice versa).",
  "intercom.stopSession": "Close explicitly. Server also auto-closes on 30s idle.",
  "irTransmitter.getInfo": "What the infrared transmitter supports.",
  "irTransmitter.learn": "Listen for an infrared code from a remote and return it.",
  "irTransmitter.send": "Transmit an infrared code, given as timings or a native code.",
  "keychain.delete": "Remove the caller's refs. Unknown refs are ignored.",
  "keychain.deleteDeviceScope": "Delete every value scoped device/<deviceId>, whatever its owner (D864). Reserved to device-manager, on the device-removed path: a driver's device-scoped secret is not anybody's once the device is gone. Answers the refs removed (never values).",
  "keychain.getState": "Whether values can be served — the save path refuses a write while locked.",
  "keychain.listMeta": "The caller's own refs, metadata only.",
  "keychain.put": "Store (or replace) the caller's value at ref. Refused while locked.",
  "keychain.releaseRecordRefs": "Release the values rows of a DROPPED record kind held, whatever the kind's owner (stale-data audit). Reserved to sqlite-settings, the engine that just deleted the rows: only refs scoped row/records:<kind>/... are accepted, and the audit names the operator it acted for. Answers a count.",
  "keychain.resolve": "Resolve the caller's refs in one round-trip. A locked keychain answers unavailable per ref — never missing, never an empty value.",
  "keychainAdmin.acknowledgeReset": "Dismiss the \"keychain was reset\" notice. Audited.",
  "keychainAdmin.deleteOrphans": "Delete refs no owner points at any more. Re-checked here; unknown is kept.",
  "keychainAdmin.downloadRecoveryKey": "The master key, base64. Audited; marks the recovery copy as taken.",
  "keychainAdmin.importSecret": "Store a value an operator tool carries over from a retired store at an addon's own ref (secret://<owner>/<scope>/<path>) and answer the ref - the D870 migration moves a camera's restream tokens this way, so they never sit in a settings row as plaintext. Audited as the operator; the caller then writes the MARKER of the ref where the value used to be.",
  "keychainAdmin.listAudit": "List recent keychain audit entries.",
  "keychainAdmin.listSecrets": "List the stored secrets without their values.",
  "keychainAdmin.purgeRetiredKeys": "Delete retired encryption keys and report how many were removed.",
  "keychainAdmin.resetKeychain": "Lost-key recovery: archive every stored value into a keychain:secrets-orphaned-<ts> table and start over with a new data key. Every secret field then reads \"not set\". Requires the typed confirmation {@link KEYCHAIN_RESET_CONFIRMATION}.",
  "keychainAdmin.resetReport": "What the last reset left to re-enter: the archived refs (owner, scope, field — never a value) that hold no value again yet. Process-held refs the hub regenerates itself (the session signing key) are not listed.",
  "keychainAdmin.reveal": "Show one value to the operator. Audited. The UI hides it again after a few seconds; nothing caches it.",
  "keychainAdmin.rotateMasterKey": "Wrap the data key under the configured primary master key.",
  "keychainAdmin.setSystemSecret": "Replace a system-held secret (no form edits it) with an operator-supplied value — e.g. importing the session signing key a pre-keychain hub kept in config.yaml, so the tokens it signed stay valid. Audited as the operator. Replacing the session signing key invalidates every token signed with the previous one.",
