  "llmRuntime.cancel": "Stop a node-side generation started with a requestId — complete or completeApple. The hub's llm.cancel forwards here with the same nodePin the generation took; before this existed a cancelled managed-local generation kept running on the node to its own timeout. Idempotent: an unknown or finished id is a no-op.",
  "llmRuntime.complete": "complete, status, listLocalModels and getDiskUsage had NO auth override — internal: true did not gate the mount (see the 2026-08-26 note on data-store-provider), so they were reachable on the AppRouter by ANY authenticated session at the default auth: 'protected', inconsistent with the rest of this cap (already auth: 'admin') and with this file's own docblock: \"the operator reaches this only through the llm cap's methods.\" The sole caller, addon-ai's runtime-client.ts, reaches every method here via ctx.api + nodePin — never tRPC — so auth: 'admin' costs it nothing; the public llm cap (which end users and non-admin sessions legitimately call for chat/generation) is untouched.",
