  "loadContribution.list": "This addon's own cost entries, computed live from state it already holds. Inert: no persistence, no sampling, no timer. It is answered on whatever beat the caller already has.",
  "localNetwork.addCustomAddress": "Add a custom address. Validated: an http(s) origin with a host, no credentials, no path, never loopback — an invalid one is refused with the reason and nothing is stored. Adding an address that already exists only updates its label.",
  "localNetwork.downloadCa": "The local CA PEM, or empty when there is none to download.",
  "localNetwork.getAddresses": "The Network page's Addresses table and every role's answer — the ONE reading of \"which address is this hub reached at, for what\": detected endpoints and custom addresses with their role flags, and per role the flagged address, the one in use and whether it is automatic. Agent deliveries and LAN devices read roles.internal; sign-in, OAuth2 and the notification centre's buttons / media / admin links read roles.publicEndpoint; nothing ranks the palette itself. scheme is the one the caller shows LAN rows in (as getConnectionEndpoints); internal and publicEndpoint are always resolved over the HTTPS palette.",
  "localNetwork.getAllowedAddresses": "Read the operator's allowlist. Empty = \"auto\" (no filter). Used by the admin UI's address selector to seed its checkbox state.",
  "localNetwork.getConnectionEndpoints": "Ordered candidate base URLs (the palette the Network tab shows). Includes LAN IPv4, stable LAN IPv6, the public tunnel, and mesh when joined. Loopback is off by default. The SDK races the subset from getViewerEndpoints, not this full list — IPv6 stays here because WebRTC ICE gathers dual-stack regardless of the HTTP race. Honours getAllowedAddresses() when set — addresses outside the allowlist are dropped (the public tunnel is still included as an escape hatch).",
  "localNetwork.getHubAddresses": "The hub's cluster and browser addresses (deprecated; use getAddresses).",
  "localNetwork.getNotificationEndpoint": "The notificationTaps role (D734): where TAPPING a notification opens. baseUrl: null means AUTO, which is the CamStack app link (D709): taps go through https://camstack.zentik.app/…?hub=<appLinkHub> and open the app. Any hub address the palette lists can be flagged instead; then a tap opens that address. Only the tap: action buttons, attachment / media links and admin links follow the publicEndpoint role (getAddresses().roles.publicEndpoint), never this one.",
  "localNetwork.getPreferred": "Auto-selected outbound interface. Heuristic: 1. Skip internal / link-local / 169.254.*. 2. Prefer LAN/wifi (real Ethernet) over docker/vpn. 3. IPv4 wins over IPv6 (compat with legacy consumers). 4. Tie-break on lowest CIDR mask (most-specific subnet). Returns null only when the host has zero non-loopback addresses. Honours getAllowedAddresses() — if the operator pinned an allowlist, only those addresses are candidates.",
  "localNetwork.getScanSubnets": "Extra subnets every scan covers besides the hub's own, as CIDR strings.",
  "localNetwork.getTlsStatus": "Live TLS material for the Network → Local access certificate card. LAN HTTP / hostname are scoped settings (the cap's own form), not a second store — this query is status, not configuration.",
  "localNetwork.getViewerEndpoints": "The appConnections role as shipped apps read it: the flagged addresses (detected or custom), or empty for AUTO — every LAN IPv4 address plus the public tunnel, never IPv6, mesh, loopback or a custom address. resolved is the set as it stands right now; the custom ones in it are also in getConnectionEndpoints, which the apps filter by it.",
  "localNetwork.list": "Return the current interface snapshot.",
  "localNetwork.regenerateCertificate": "Issue a new leaf under the existing local CA. Disabled in uploaded mode.",
  "localNetwork.removeCustomAddress": "Remove a custom address. Its role flags go with it (those roles turn automatic).",
  "localNetwork.resetAllowlistToBestMatch": "Re-run the boot heuristic over the current interface snapshot and atomically replace the allowlist with the result. Useful after a major network change (new dock, new VPN, IP rebound) when the operator wants to wipe their manual edits and start over from the auto-detected best matches.",
  "localNetwork.revertToGeneratedCertificate": "Return to the generated local CA. The uploaded certificate stays stored (D873).",
  "localNetwork.scanNetwork": "The LAN discovery engine. Every provider that declared discovery modes (device-provider.getDiscoveryModes) is scanned in ONE pass: a single mDNS browse for the union of service types, one WS-Discovery probe, one SSDP search per target and one sweep that visits each host once and runs every http-probe of every provider. Subnets scanned = the hub's own non-internal IPv4 /24s ∪ the saved list (getScanSubnets) ∪ subnets. A bad CIDR, or more than 4096 hosts in total, refuses the scan.",
  "localNetwork.setAddressRole": "Flag (enabled: true) or unflag an address for a role. For a single-valued role, flagging moves the flag off every other address. baseUrl: null returns the role to automatic. The address must be a row of the table (detected, custom, or the app link for notificationTaps); publicEndpoint on a plain-http address is refused unless acceptInsecureHttp, and never takes the app link.",
  "localNetwork.setAllowedAddresses": "Replace the allowlist atomically. Persisted via the addon store (kernel-managed) so it survives restarts. Pass [] to revert to auto mode.",
  "localNetwork.setNotificationEndpoint": "Set the base URL used in links inside notifications; null clears it.",
  "localNetwork.setScanSubnets": "Replace the saved extra subnets (a cluster setting). Each entry is IPv4 CIDR, at most a /22; the list is refused when it is invalid or its hosts would exceed the scan cap.",
  "localNetwork.setViewerEndpoints": "Set the base URLs the viewer apps reach the hub on.",
  "localNetwork.uploadCertificate": "Replace the served material with operator-supplied PEMs. A certificate that does not lead to a public CA must come with its CA certificate, validated and kept for Download CA (D873).",
  "localNetwork.useStoredUploadedCertificate": "Serve the kept upload again after \"Revert to generated\" (D873). Refused when none is kept.",
