  "serverManagement.installDesktopUpdate": "Ask the desktop app hosting this node to install its DOWNLOADED update and restart. The request is a file in the node's data dir (the node may be a Windows service, not Electron's child); the app consumes it once. accepted: true means the request was WRITTEN — the app restarting is observed afterwards on desktopApp.version, not promised here. Refused with a named reason when not an electron shell, the app's state is absent or stale, or nothing is downloaded.",
  "serverManagement.restartServer": "Plain process restart of the node's root process — no version change. The supervisor (docker restart policy / launchd / Electron main) relaunches and the starter loads the SAME active version. Refused while a stage is in flight or a version is already staged awaiting restart (use apply/rollback instead, so the pending version is not skipped).",
