  "ssoBridge.signBridgeToken": "internal: true did not gate the mount (see the 2026-08-26 note on data-store-provider) — signBridgeToken was reachable on the AppRouter by ANY authenticated session at the default auth: 'protected'. The claims (including isAdmin) are CALLER- SUPPLIED: an unprivileged session could have minted its own isAdmin: true bridge token and redeemed it at /api/auth/sso/finish to become admin — a full privilege escalation through the exact surface this cap exists to close (see the module docblock). Every real caller (oauth-grants.ts, main.ts registration, the OIDC addon) reaches this through ctx.api / the in-process registry — never through tRPC — so auth: 'admin' costs those callers nothing.",
