  "streamBroker.previewDerivedEncode": "The effective encode a derived-stream profile WOULD run with, computed by the same function the broker uses when it starts the encode, against the source params the broker has already probed for deviceId. Lets an editor show the final geometry, fps, bitrate and ffmpeg argv live while the operator edits. source defaults to the high profile slot. { kind: 'no-source' } when nothing has been probed yet — never a guess.",
  "streamBroker.probeStream": "Force a one-shot probe of a single source stream: transiently dial the broker (a warmup consumer), capture a fresh BrokerStats snapshot for the per-stream \"Probed\" settings field, then release. Wakes a suspended (incl. battery) stream for a few seconds. summary is the rendered probed-values string; probed is false if the stream never reached streaming within the timeout.",
